# React State, Props & Scale Performance

> Apply on every frontend change. Prefer simple code that stays fast at 500–1000+ items.

---

## State Placement (lowest scope wins)

| Scope | Use when | Avoid |
|-------|----------|-------|
| `useState` in component/hook | Only this UI needs it (`isOpen`, `draft`) | Lifting "just in case" |
| Lifted state / callback props | 2+ siblings share read+write | Prop drilling >2 levels |
| Domain context (`BookContext`, `CanvasSettingsContext`) | Many distant consumers, read-heavy | One mega-context for everything |
| `useRef` | Values that must NOT re-render (`isIntersectingRef`, canvas refs, cancel flags) | Storing UI that should display |
| Pure `utils/` | Deterministic transforms, validation, indexing | React imports in utils |

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — duplicated + derivable
const [items, setItems] = useState<Item[]>([])
const [activeCount, setActiveCount] = useState(0)

// ✅ GOOD — single source, derive
const [items, setItems] = useState<Item[]>([])
const activeCount = useMemo(() => items.filter((i) => i.isActive).length, [items])
```

**Reducer** when one action updates 3+ related fields. **Never** mirror server data in context if a hook already owns it.

---

## Props Design

- Define prop interfaces in `types/*.types.ts` — not inline in components.
- UI components: **data + callbacks only** — no canvas/DOM/API side effects.
- Hooks return stable shapes: `{ state, actions }` or `{ bindings }` — containers spread once.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — new object every render → memo child always re-renders
<RowItem config={{ id, onSelect: () => select(id) }} />

// ✅ GOOD — stable callback from hook + primitive props
const { selectItem } = actions
<RowItem id={id} isSelected={selectedId === id} onSelect={selectItem} />
```

- **Max 3–4 top-level props** on leaf UI — group the rest into one typed object from the hook.
- Do not pass entire parent state when child needs one field.
- `children` / composition over boolean prop explosion (`renderX`, `showY`, `hideZ`).

---

## Re-render Control (targeted, not blanket)

| Tool | Use when |
|------|----------|
| `React.memo` | List/grid row components rendered 50+ times (`FabricCanvasItem`) |
| `useCallback` | Callback passed to `memo` child or effect dependency |
| `useMemo` | O(n) filter/sort/map on large arrays; expensive object builds |
| Ref | Read latest value in async loop without stale closure re-subscribe |

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — memo everywhere (adds compare cost, obscures data flow)
export const Label = memo(({ text }: { text: string }) => <span>{text}</span>)

// ✅ GOOD — memo at list boundary only
export const FabricCanvasItem = memo(function FabricCanvasItem(props) { ... })
```

**Do not** `useCallback`/`useMemo` by default — add when profiling or list scale demands it.

---

## Large Collections (500–1000+ pages/items)

Follow existing editor patterns:

1. **Lazy mount** — lightweight shell + heavy child only when near viewport (`FabricCanvasItem` → `FabricCanvasItemActive`).
2. **Hysteresis** — different activate/deactivate margins to avoid mount/dispose thrash on scroll.
3. **Index structures** — `Map<number, T>` / `Set` for O(1) lookup; never `.find()` in hot loops.
4. **Chunk + yield** — long sync work calls `yieldToMainThread()` between chunks; show progress UI.
5. **Batch updates** — one `setState` / one store commit per chunk, not per item.
6. **Virtualize** when DOM node count is the bottleneck (thumbnails, long lists).

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — bounded memory at scale
for (const job of chunk) {
  if (cancelRef.current) break
  await processJob(job)
  await yieldToMainThread()
}
```

---

## Memory

- **Cleanup** every `useEffect`: listeners, `IntersectionObserver`, timers, `URL.revokeObjectURL`.
- **Dispose** heavy instances on unmount (Fabric canvas, workers, large buffers).
- **Persist + release** — save to store, drop live instance when off-screen (visibility hook pattern).
- **No unbounded caches** in React state — cap size or use LRU in module scope with explicit eviction.
- **Avoid** spreading/cloning large nested objects in render; update only changed slice.

---

## Complexity Limits

- One hook = one domain (`use-bulk-puzzle-generation`, `use-canvas-download`).
- Orchestrator hook calls pure utils; utils have zero React hooks.
- Max **3–4** `useState` per hook — merge related fields or use `useReducer`.
- No inline logic in JSX beyond trivial ternaries — extract named handler or hook action.
- Effects: **one concern per effect**; deps must be complete and minimal.

---

## Pre-Change Checklist (frontend)

- [ ] State at lowest scope? No derivable duplicate state?
- [ ] Props minimal, stable, typed in `types/`?
- [ ] List rows memoized? Callbacks stable for memo children?
- [ ] Large loops chunked + yielding? Progress feedback for user?
- [ ] Lookups O(1)? No full-array scan in hot path?
- [ ] Effects cleaned up? Heavy refs released off-screen?
- [ ] Would 1000 items still feel responsive?
